  <Patch Id="NCdbcDGRIQBtzDa8Qsjck9">
    <Canvas Id="x446rPzz3AoiThXTUwistN" DefaultCategory="Main" BordersChecked="false" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,180" Id="rm9eKIEmpaF75V7Im2Uaem">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <CategoryReference Kind="Category" Name="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="1FhshkNfPiVAOgARb5Xv4o">
        <Canvas Id="VakVFEiIWqygU31A4k81W4" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="87lNBG4e1T4NB97adIxa8G" Bounds="85,16,420,52" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="How To Chain Shader Effects">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">25</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="7FWqnojcfaXzr3VWh4Tmpi" Bounds="85,85,830,122" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Filter shaders from a qtshaders folder also appear in Qt.Effects and chain like Blur or DropShadow:&#xD;&#xA;- The order is the data flow, like Stride TextureFX: the first node of the chain works first, the node at the Effect pin works last.&#xD;&#xA;- Neighbouring Blur, DropShadow, ColorAdjust, Colorize and Mask nodes merge into ONE layer (one MultiEffect). A shader node ends such a run and gets a layer of its own.&#xD;&#xA;- Reorder the nodes and the picture changes: left and right use the same three nodes in opposite order.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="6Rha6yqGSHebm8tcNGbspp" Bounds="85,222,830,160" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- A shader node never shares a layer, so a shader between Blur and DropShadow costs three layers; Blur and DropShadow on one side of the shader would share one.&#xD;&#xA;- If a shader draws beyond the element (RGBSplit shifts the colors outwards), set @padding in the head of the .frag, in DIP: one number or left, top, right, bottom. The layer grows by it, otherwise the effect may be clipped at the element bounds.&#xD;&#xA;- Size, Transform and Interaction stay on the element. A shader node shows compile errors with line numbers at its Error output.&#xD;&#xA;- How filter shader files become nodes: see HowTo Create Shader Nodes from Files.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="bn3X8N66xNNaKlyWGxHsrc" Bounds="100,440,450,46" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="1  Blur -&gt; RGBSplit -&gt; DropShadow: the blurred text is split into its color channels, the shadow follows the result.">
